{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788391762405967001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"eagleeyed-commutable-mantisray","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6ba9dd58abf1abfe5e6f92a76325d05bd7fe266dbabdba828c696167e8369b51","event_uuid":"e862fb29-6e4c-49f6-aa90-da02f7efc986","position":{"commit_sha":"702c43eb688c160d1e4e6d1fa5647d2e96c6f6be","position":"1788388096425437001-e862fb29-6e4c-49f6-aa90-da02f7efc986"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"88c121f0bf1bbff77e5748711c8e7ac60d771212eb53132f573299ee2b414ccf","event_uuid":"288ae69c-26c3-409d-b417-ba283987d259","position":{"commit_sha":"9e0e9c6b51a0ad9a1cfebac7ab18e49724fcd6b3","position":"1788388116116882001-288ae69c-26c3-409d-b417-ba283987d259"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788388096425437001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Why this exists\n\n`src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` is at **exactly 800 lines** — the hard cap. Sibling\n`elfin-decagonal-polarbear` (F11, mirror F11) must add a `warn_cross_session` flag to `Route`\nand fold it into `derive_policy_sets`, which cannot be done without going over.\n\nThis is filed as its own ticket deliberately. Splitting a module is a structural change with\nits own review surface; folding it into a mirror-remediation change would put an unrelated\nrefactor inside a change whose reviewed plan is about single-sourcing a policy set, and would\nmake both harder to review and to revert.\n\n**This has already bitten this epic twice.** `_commands/composer.py` was likewise at exactly\n800; the F3 change added an import and a comment, took the whole stack to `Verified -1`, and\nthe recovery mis-amended a commit and opened a duplicate Gerrit change. F7 then had to express\nits fix in ZERO net lines to fit. That is code shaped around a cap rather than around meaning.\n\nFour other `src/rebar` files sit at exactly 800 today (`llm/plan_review/sizing.py`,\n`llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`, `_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py`,\n`_commands/composer.py`), so this is a general hazard; this ticket addresses only the one the\nepic is blocked on.\n\n## The seam\n\nNot a mechanical cut to hit a number. `_registry.py` holds three clusters, and one is already\nself-contained:\n\n- **route TABLE construction** — `_core_factory`, `_reads_init_only`, `_simple_read_groups`,\n  `_lifecycle`, `_writes_full`, `_intercepts`, `_bridge_and_arms`, `_build_routes` (~520 lines)\n- **types + lookup** — `Route`, `Finding`, `_index`, `route_for`, `derive_policy_sets`\n- **registry VALIDATION** (`:684-795`, ~112 lines) — `_is_valid_reference`, the six `_check_*`\n  functions, `_CHECKS`, `validate`\n\nThe validation cluster is the seam: its functions call only each other, take\n`routes: tuple[Route, ...]` as a PARAMETER, and yield `Finding`. It reads the registry; it does\nnot build it. Extracting it leaves `_registry.py` at roughly 688 with ~112 lines of headroom,\nand the new module lands well above the 100-LOC floor, so this is a split along an existing\ncall-graph seam rather than one invented for the cap.\n\n`validate` and `Finding` must stay importable from `rebar._cli._registry` — `test_capabilities`,\n`test_cli_registry` and `test_cli_registry_dispatch` all import them from there. The in-tree\nprecedent for the back-compat re-export is `gate_dispatch.py`, which re-exports the\n`plan_review_recovery` cluster and documents the re-export as load-bearing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: the validation cluster moves to a new `src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py`, and\n      `_registry.py` is under the cap with real headroom. Verified by `wc -l` on both and by the\n      CI module-size gate passing.\n- [ ] AC2: `validate` and `Finding` remain importable from `rebar._cli._registry`. Verified by\n      the existing importers (`test_capabilities`, `test_cli_registry`,\n      `test_cli_registry_dispatch`) passing untouched.\n- [ ] AC3: behavior is byte-identical — the same findings, in the same order, for the same\n      routes. Verified by a test asserting `tuple(validate(ROUTES))` is unchanged and by\n      `validate()` still returning empty on the committed registry.\n- [ ] AC4: the new module is above the 100-LOC floor, so this is a seam extraction and not a\n      fragment. Verified by `wc -l`.\n- [ ] AC5: no route definition, alias, or policy set is altered. Verified by a test asserting\n      the `ROUTES` name/alias sets and every `derive_policy_sets` output are identical to\n      before, so the split cannot have moved behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"registry or capabilities or dispatch or cli\" -q` — AC2, AC3,\n  AC5 and the existing registry suites.\n- `wc -l src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py` — AC1, AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"the validation cluster moves out; the module keeps route construction, types and lookup, plus a back-compat re-export of validate and Finding"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py","reason":"new: the extracted registry-validation cluster (_is_valid_reference, the six _check_* functions, _CHECKS, validate)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_split.py","reason":"the oracle: identical findings and identical policy sets across the split, and the back-compat import path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bc66-4827-355a-43bd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Split _cli/_registry.py at its validation seam so the registry has headroom","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e862fb29-6e4c-49f6-aa90-da02f7efc986","288ae69c-26c3-409d-b417-ba283987d259"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788391762405967001,"uuid":"d1e5e7e8-2c16-49ec-90f5-b4f0b3a63843"}